WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:03.280
What is the most dangerous&nbsp;
creature in the universe?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:08.800
Here on planet Earth there are creatures that have&nbsp;
hardly evolved since prehistoric eras like sharks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:14.960
crocodiles, and snakes… perfect biological&nbsp;
killing machines. But then again, the animal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:21.120
kingdom is nothing when compared to the menagerie&nbsp;
of creatures contained by the SCP Foundation.&nbsp;

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:28.320
So, once again, what is the most dangerous&nbsp;
creature in the universe? Is it SCP-682?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:34.240
The damage regenerating reptile with a hatred&nbsp;
for all other forms of life? Or is it The Scarlet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:40.480
King? Or is the Broken God more deserving of that&nbsp;
title? Maybe the answer still lies elsewhere, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:45.840
thankfully, there is one SCP in the Foundation’s&nbsp;
archives that might not be the most dangerous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:51.920
itself, but teaches us a very important lesson&nbsp;
about what the most dangerous entity truly is.&nbsp;

00:00:52.480 --> 00:01:00.160
This is the story of SCP-001, The Spiral Path.
An important distinction, before we go any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:04.800
further: SCP-001 doesn’t refer&nbsp;
to a single creature, object,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:10.880
or entity, but rather a collection of various&nbsp;
anomalies contained by the SCP Foundation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:17.280
It is unclear why there are multiple files&nbsp;
collected under the shared designation of SCP-001.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:21.600
Some believe these anomalies are some of the&nbsp;
earliest ever contained by the Foundation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:25.120
encountered before they introduced&nbsp;
their current numbering system.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:31.600
There is also the theory that this is intentional&nbsp;
misdirection, that the multiple SCP-001 files&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:37.840
are an attempt by the Foundation to conceal&nbsp;
secret information about the true SCP-001.&nbsp;

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:43.360
Anomalies sharing the name SCP-001 include&nbsp;
the infamous, aforementioned Scarlet King,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:48.640
a powerful eldritch being intent on ending&nbsp;
all creation. Another anomalous being with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:53.680
similar levels of destructive power is the Gate&nbsp;
Guardian, believed to be an angel standing at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.680 --> 00:02:01.600
entrance to the Garden of Eden, it too goes by the&nbsp;
name SCP-001. But, for the purposes of this video,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:08.320
we will be using SCP-001 to refer to something&nbsp;
otherwise codenamed The Spiral Path. And while it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:16.080
is not a creature in and of itself, SCP-001 does&nbsp;
yield one answer to that important question: What&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:23.520
is the most dangerous creature in the universe?
On paper, SCP-001 does not seem to be much,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:28.320
and it certainly doesn’t appear to be any&nbsp;
sort of threat. As its nickname suggests,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:34.720
The Spiral Path is exactly that. Located&nbsp;
deep in a wooded area known only as Site 0,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:41.360
SCP-001 is a gravel path in the shape of a spiral.&nbsp;
Your first thought at hearing that might be,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:46.000
“what could be so important about a path?”
If someone were to find themselves walking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:52.480
along The Spiral Path, traveling clockwise around&nbsp;
the gravel, then they will find that… nothing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:58.640
happens. It’s just a normal path with slight&nbsp;
inclines and declines as one traverses it. If&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:05.440
one should walk counterclockwise around it though,&nbsp;
then they will begin to experience SCP-001’s first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:11.280
anomalous effect. The path will begin to feel&nbsp;
as if it is sloping uphill, getting steeper and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:16.480
steeper. When they reach the beginning of the path&nbsp;
again, a person will still as if they are walking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:22.800
endlessly uphill. All this while, the path itself&nbsp;
does not move or change in form or altitude.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:30.160
To put it simply, walking one way around SCP-001&nbsp;
causes it to behave normally. Walking the other,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:36.080
the path does not adhere to the laws of physics.
You may well be thinking, “is that all?” On a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:41.440
surface level, The Spiral Path does appear&nbsp;
to be just an unmoving, low-threat anomaly.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:46.960
While it may not be as aggressive or malicious&nbsp;
as some of the SCP Foundation’s rogues gallery,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:52.400
it is still a spatial anomaly that defies all&nbsp;
Euclidean geometry. That might sound like small&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:57.440
potatoes when compared to everything the SCP&nbsp;
Foundation has faced over the years. But bear in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.440 --> 00:04:04.800
mind, if The Spiral Path is truly SCP-001, and the&nbsp;
very first anomaly that the Foundation learned of,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:09.360
then a simple path that ignores the ordinary&nbsp;
laws of space and time would have been a major&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.360 --> 00:04:14.800
discovery in the organization’s earliest days.
But why would they still keep The Spiral Path&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:20.960
so heavily guarded all these years later?
SCP-001 is kept behind a maximum security&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:26.800
fence that has been constructed all the way around&nbsp;
the perimeter of Site 0. At all times, the SCP&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:32.320
Foundation keeps no less than five fully armed&nbsp;
members of security personnel on site to keep&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:38.080
watch over The Spiral Path and make sure that no&nbsp;
one approaches it who isn’t authorized to. There&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:44.000
is a small metal plaque too, bearing an unknown&nbsp;
inscription on it. Special Containment Procedures&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:49.840
for SCP-001 state that this plaque is to be kept&nbsp;
in good condition, and it should be immediately&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.840 --> 00:04:55.680
reported if it shows any signs of damage.
A Foundation physics laboratory is also located&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.680 --> 00:05:01.280
nearby, where research staff tirelessly&nbsp;
conduct scientific tests on SCP-001&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:05.840
and its anomalous properties. So, there’s&nbsp;
definitely something more to The Spiral Path&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:11.680
than a simple stroll around it would tell you.
Attached to SCP-001’s file is an item referred&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:18.720
to as Document 001-O5. Written by high ranking&nbsp;
Foundation researcher Doctor Everett Mann,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:24.000
any prospective or new members of the O5&nbsp;
Council are required to read this document and,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:30.000
from the events it details, learn the truth.
Not just the truth about The Spiral Path,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:36.320
but the truth about the SCP Foundation itself.
Doctor Mann begins this file by explaining to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.320 --> 00:05:41.440
the reader that either he or one of the original&nbsp;
founders of the SCP Foundation must have died,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:47.360
and the person reading has been appointed as a&nbsp;
successor. Whether his death was caused by an SCP,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:52.400
an operative from another anomalous organization&nbsp;
like the Global Occult Coalition, or “getting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.400 --> 00:05:57.760
a little close to the flame”, Mann states that&nbsp;
old age definitely wouldn’t be what killed him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.760 --> 00:06:02.320
He writes, “We took care of that, didn’t we?”
Whether he means that he and the rest of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:06.560
“old guard” are somehow immortal, or just&nbsp;
working for the Foundation would likely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.560 --> 00:06:12.720
mean dying before reaching old age, is unclear.
But, Doctor Mann’s next statement is one that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:17.600
changes the very way we view the Foundation&nbsp;
and its entire purpose. “We have never&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:24.400
‘discovered’ an SCP in the entire history of&nbsp;
the Foundation.” According to Document 001-O5,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:30.640
every instance of an anomalous creature,&nbsp;
entity or object, is entirely staged.&nbsp;

00:06:30.640 --> 00:06:36.640
He then goes on to describe Aaron Siegel, a gifted&nbsp;
physicist that Doctor Mann regarded very highly.&nbsp;

00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:41.680
“I believe that his name would be there with&nbsp;
Edison, Einstein, and Hawking. I knew him very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.680 --> 00:06:47.680
well. He was, and may still be, my brother.”
The pair evidently shared a close personal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.680 --> 00:06:54.640
connection, and it was Siegel who first discovered&nbsp;
SCP-001. During a hike, Aaron stumbled upon The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:59.840
Spiral Path, noticing that no matter how far&nbsp;
uphill he seemed to travel, his elevation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.840 --> 00:07:05.920
never once changed, only for him to end up back&nbsp;
at the start of the path. Being a physicist,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.920 --> 00:07:11.200
Siegel quickly realized how this unassuming&nbsp;
gravel path did not conform to Euclidean geometry,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:15.840
that it did not fit within the laws of nature.
Constructing a small wooden shack nearby,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:22.080
Aaron Siegel began to study the properties of&nbsp;
The Spiral Path. Equation after equation, hours&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:28.480
spent examining every variable and experimenting&nbsp;
with his findings. Until something unforeseen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.480 --> 00:07:35.760
happened: Aaron created an SCP, a key that had&nbsp;
the innate ability to open any lock. Nowadays,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:41.680
that same key is still in the Foundation’s&nbsp;
possession, under the designation SCP-005.&nbsp;

00:07:42.240 --> 00:07:47.680
Slowly, Aaron began to bring others into the fold,&nbsp;
trusted colleagues and other scientific minds.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.680 --> 00:07:53.200
Among them was, of course, Doctor Everett Mann,&nbsp;
who was still a medical student at Harvard at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:59.600
time. This brain trust, a think tank composed of&nbsp;
only a select few, they were the very beginning.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.600 --> 00:08:05.120
The ones who founded the SCP Foundation.
Using their own fortunes and funding from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.120 --> 00:08:10.320
Thomas Carter, the group continued with Siegel’s&nbsp;
experiments. The scientists had high hopes for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.320 --> 00:08:14.960
what they could achieve, planning to change&nbsp;
the world for the better. Feeding the hungry,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.960 --> 00:08:20.320
providing shelter to the homeless, curing&nbsp;
the sick, and even cheating death itself.&nbsp;

00:08:20.320 --> 00:08:25.280
In the beginning, this proto-Foundation started&nbsp;
small. Their goals were noble, but could not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.280 --> 00:08:30.480
realistically be achieved overnight. They tried&nbsp;
to make items that would improve life, such as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:36.800
fountain of youth, a partially sentient Civil War&nbsp;
statue, and an extremely bouncy ball. Better known&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:46.080
to the Foundation today as SCP-006, SCP-011 and&nbsp;
SCP-018 respectively. But then this new Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:51.760
began to grow, with more organization and a&nbsp;
secret facility. And with that expansion, came&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:58.160
emboldened scientists, eager to change the world.
The group began working on human test subjects,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.160 --> 00:09:04.320
volunteers and drifters that soon became SCPs.
The Spiral Path was not just a break in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.320 --> 00:09:09.840
fabric of reality. In a metaphorical sense, it&nbsp;
referred to the spiraling path the newly formed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.840 --> 00:09:16.560
Foundation itself was on. Every discovery they&nbsp;
made led to another, and that to another still.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.560 --> 00:09:23.520
Until things started to go wrong. During the&nbsp;
continuing experiments, Dr Mann created SCP-008,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.520 --> 00:09:29.200
a deadly zombie plague capable of infecting&nbsp;
anyone with one hundred percent lethality. More&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.200 --> 00:09:35.440
and more of the founders were so invested in their&nbsp;
projects, that the results were often nightmarish.&nbsp;

00:09:35.440 --> 00:09:40.720
The Foundation needed help, that came when&nbsp;
Thomas Carter showed their work to the military&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.720 --> 00:09:47.120
in exchange for additional funding and personnel.
The SCP Foundation expanded even further, becoming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.120 --> 00:09:53.200
an international organization and bringing in&nbsp;
new researchers and staff. In some instances,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.200 --> 00:09:58.480
the founders would arrange for the anomalies they&nbsp;
had created to be “found” by the new recruits,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.480 --> 00:10:04.160
other times they would fabricate reports,&nbsp;
changing the details of how things like SCP-008&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:10.160
or the fountain of youth were first discovered.&nbsp;
Anything the founders said was simply now a fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.160 --> 00:10:13.840
no one questioned them.
Even then, problems still arose.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:18.480
Founding members broke away from the SCP&nbsp;
Foundation, some even creating splinter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.480 --> 00:10:23.680
groups that would later become infamous Groups&nbsp;
of Interest. The Foundation’s directive shifted,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:29.040
now focusing on the containment of anomalies,&nbsp;
as yet more were created through darker means.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.040 --> 00:10:36.000
SCP-231 was taken from an orphanage, Doctor Mann&nbsp;
himself vivisected a small boy who then became&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:42.480
SCP-610, the Flesh That Hates. And there&nbsp;
were more still; Abel, the blood pond,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.480 --> 00:10:49.280
and even the Hard To Destroy Reptile. All of&nbsp;
them were the creation of the Foundation itself.&nbsp;

00:10:49.280 --> 00:10:54.160
But through it all, Doctor Mann wrote, he was&nbsp;
never afraid of the path that the Foundation was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.160 --> 00:10:59.360
on. He was never even afraid of all the monsters&nbsp;
and abominations that he and the other founders&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.360 --> 00:11:06.880
had secretly created by studying SCP-001. What&nbsp;
truly scared him were the anomalies the Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.880 --> 00:11:12.720
didn’t create. There were some that would just&nbsp;
appear in containment one day, even if they hadn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.720 --> 00:11:17.920
been there before. They would seem like they had&nbsp;
always been there. Doctor Mann closes Document&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.920 --> 00:11:25.520
001-O5 with the realization that he and the other&nbsp;
founders simply were not in control anymore.&nbsp;

00:11:25.520 --> 00:11:31.200
The tale of Doctor Mann and the other founders of&nbsp;
the SCP Foundation is one of noble intentions that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.200 --> 00:11:36.560
ultimately became corrupted. At first, the&nbsp;
founders created SCPs that they hoped would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:36.560 --> 00:11:44.800
benefit humanity. But then came the mistakes,&nbsp;
the accidents, the monsters, like SCP-008,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:44.800 --> 00:11:53.040
SCP-610, and even SCP-682. The Foundation lied&nbsp;
to the governments and militaries of the world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:53.040 --> 00:11:58.960
claiming they’d found these SCPs - not&nbsp;
created them - and in return, they received&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:58.960 --> 00:12:06.080
funding and staff to expand, allowing the SCP&nbsp;
Foundation to grow to become what it is today.&nbsp;

00:12:06.080 --> 00:12:10.640
Dr Mann posits that at this point, the&nbsp;
Foundation was no longer in control,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:10.640 --> 00:12:15.520
but perhaps they never were.
And all of this stems back from one,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:15.520 --> 00:12:21.360
singular starting point: The Spiral Path. It&nbsp;
might be impossible to truly know how many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:21.360 --> 00:12:29.040
anomalies and SCPs the Foundation created, just&nbsp;
from researching SCP-001. Only the O5 Council&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:29.040 --> 00:12:34.960
will ever know exactly how many of the founders’&nbsp;
discoveries they themselves were responsible for.&nbsp;

00:12:34.960 --> 00:12:39.280
And now you know the answer to what’s the&nbsp;
most dangerous creature in the universe.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:39.280 --> 00:12:44.960
It’s regular people, dabbling with something&nbsp;
they could never hope to fully understand.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:44.960 --> 00:12:51.760
Starting with the hope to change the world, only&nbsp;
to create monsters that might one day destroy it.&nbsp;

00:12:51.760 --> 00:12:56.480
Now go check out “SCP-001 -&nbsp;
Which is the Real 001?” and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:56.480 --> 00:13:03.840
“SCP-001 - The Scarlet King” for more&nbsp;
on the legendary SCP-001 designation!

